        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7d947bf4-1e27-568a-babb-127d18859416",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Guggenheim Museum SoHo, Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum, Solomon R. Guggenheim Foundation, Fulcrum Gallery\n- People: Arata Isozaki, Hilla von Rebay, Valerie Monroe Shakespeare\n- Places: SoHo, Upper East Side, Manhattan, New York City\n- Topics: art museums, art galleries\n\nFacts:\n- In 1939, the Solomon R. Guggenheim Foundation established the Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum as the Museum of Non-Objective Painting under the guidance of its first director, Hilla von Rebay.\n- In January 1993, Valerie Monroe Shakespeare opened Fulcrum Gallery underneath the Guggenheim Museum SoHo in New York City.\n- The Guggenheim Museum SoHo was a branch of the Guggenheim Museum designed by Arata Isozaki at the corner of Broadway and Prince Street in Manhattan's SoHo neighborhood in New York City.\n- The Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum is an art museum at 1071 Fifth Avenue on the corner of East 89th Street in Manhattan's Upper East Side neighborhood in New York City.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
